WEBVTT

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.730
You'll definitely remember, Kaito!

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.210
Seira!

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:12.020
Seira, I'll definitely get your orange heart shards back!

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.770
The Thief of Memories

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:29.460
It's a shame that we have to go home now, but if we don't, the citizens of our kingdoms will worry.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.900
I see. You're leaving already.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.700
It's going to get a bit lonely.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.800
Even though the time we spent was short, it was really fun.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.410
I didn't meet any great guys.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.840
I told you!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.190
So, Lucia, Hanon, Rina.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.440
Please take care of yourselves.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.540
See you later!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.670
Goodbye!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.430
Be careful!

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.310
If you find any hot guys, tell us!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.120
Aww. Coco, Karen, and Noelle have returned to their own kingdoms.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.690
Summer vacation is ending just like that.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.990
Where is the sound of that music box coming from?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.700
Hello, Rihito-san!

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.080
Lucia-chan!

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.300
Oh! A music box.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.900
So that was the music I heard.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.100
Y-Yeah.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.640
I was planning on getting rid of it.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.590
Getting rid of it?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.000
You're going to burn it?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:44.720
Yeah.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.140
How could you? This music box is beautiful.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.700
Rihito-san, if you don't want it, can I have it?

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.440
No, you can't!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.410
Rihito-san.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.940
No... uhh, I'm sorry.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.620
Oh no! I'm sorry too for giving you trouble.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.940
Onii-sama! Where are you?

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.120
I'm giving this to you. Take it and go home.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.190
Huh? Didn't you just say I couldn't have it, Rihito-san?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:10.950
Just do it!

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.120
See you later.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:12.940
Eh?

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.810
Mikaru, I'm coming.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.030
Is it fine for me to take this?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.480
Did Rihito-san give you this? I'm so jealous, Lucia.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.170
It looks like an antique.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.700
The design is very intricate. It's worth a lot of money.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.480
Maybe Rihito-san is falling in love with you, Lucia.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:35.650
No way!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.830
He was going to burn it, so I asked him to give it to me.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.880
Burn it? Why would he do that?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.960
I don't know.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.450
Huh? The drawer won't open.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.490
It's like it's stuck on something.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.720
What was that noise?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.170
How cruel.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.570
The kitchen's been trashed.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.380
What happened here?

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.470
Taki-san, that shadow just now was...

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:04.110
Yeah. It's a burglar, no doubt about it.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.890
Eh!? A burglar?

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.910
W-What in the world is going on?

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.350
Just now, Taki-san saw a shadow in her crystal ball.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.850
So that must have been the burglar that was here.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.970
But that's weird.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.510
The lights are all on.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.710
Why would a burglar come to a place with people still inside?

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.370
You do have a point.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:41.690
Among all the things worth stealing in the Pearl Piari, the most valuable thing would be my beauty.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:48.310
I know! Lucia, didn't you just bring back an antique music box?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.330
Yeah. What about it?

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.350
Maybe the burglar was after the antique music box?

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:59.430
Some antiques are worth a lot.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.140
Eh!?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:00.980
Are you serious!?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:06.540
It doesn't matter what the burglar is after. We have to deal with him at all costs.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.510
Everyone, put everything valuable in the dining room.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.410
Okay!

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.610
Understood, Rina.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.220
Kaito.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:18.730
Hmm?

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:22.660
Kaito, it's really late. Where are you going?

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.050
I'm heading to my place for a bit.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.260
It's getting colder. I should probably get some clothes that are more suitable for fall.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.500
You don't have to get your fall clothes.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.070
You could borrow some from Onii-sama.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.010
Mikaru...

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:48.070
Kaito?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.020
Don't worry. I'll be back soon.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.050
Really, Kaito?

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.050
Would I lie to you?

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.290
Okay, I'm leaving.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.380
You better come back soon, Kaito.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:00.980
I will.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:04.930
Kaito...

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:27.050
It seems that Mikeru-sama's servants aren't up to the task of dealing with the Mermaid Princesses.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:32.760
We didn't anticipate that the Mermaid Princesses would be able to counter our efforts.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.610
Yeah, and the condition of Mikeru-sama's body is getting worse.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.000
I'm not sure if there is another way to...

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.370
You don't need to worry about that.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.770
I will give you the power to alleviate Mikeru's suffering.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.150
T-This is...

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:57.130
The Mermaid Princesses will be no match for us as long Mikeru can be stabilized.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:57.790
Yes, sir!

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:07.180
Everything that's valuable is here.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:07.840
Yeah!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.500
I've brought the music box here as well.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.420
So, Taki-san and I will be guarding the front door.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.090
Hanon-chan and Rina-chan, please take care of the back door.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.230
Lucia, you're responsible for watching the dining room.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:18.860
Understood?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.090
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:24.520
T-This is...

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.690
What is it?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.580
Taki-san, what's wrong?

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:31.180
There's no doubt about it. The burglar is hiding nearby!

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.170
Eh!? You're kidding, right?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.000
These days, who would be idiotic enough to fall for a trap like this?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.580
He would have to be a real blockhead to fall for this, that's for sure.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.150
If a suspicious person trips this, the empty cans should alert us.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.590
That's our Rina-san!

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.010
Incredible...

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.670
Did the two of you make this, Nikora-san and Taki-san?

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:17.330
Pretty much.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.450
What is it? What was that noise?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.190
Lucia, look at this trap!

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:25.260
Nikora-san and Taki-san made it.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:27.080
Ah! Incredible!

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.190
Now, there's no way the thief will beat us!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.590
Yeah!

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:37.250
But Taki-san, doesn't this trap only trigger after the door is opened?

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.000
Don't worry about that!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.880
I've divined another trap for the burglar.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.700
Gyaaah!

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.230
What was that noise?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.990
Maybe it's the burglar.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:49.660
Let's take a look.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:50.270
Okay!

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.010
W-What {in the hell }is this?

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:53.990
Oww!

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.180
Nagisa?

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.350
What {in the  }are you doing here?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.470
Never mind that! Just help me get out of here, Hanon!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.420
Oww! Oww! Oww!

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:08.250
Okay, what {in the  }were you doing?

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.320
Why {in the  }did you come to our home?

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.590
Why, you ask? Summer vacation is almost over.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.930
I thought that maybe you didn't finish your summer homework.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.030
So, I figured I could help you out.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:25.360
I'm very sorry, but I haven't degraded to the point where I need a first-year student to do my homework!

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.770
That's not important!

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.600
We're good friends.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.070
Why you little{ er}...

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.850
Apparently, you have a boyfriend who was worried about your summer homework.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.340
How wonderful!

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:37.590
If we're talking about burglars, then he's a thief of love.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:43.880
You inconvenienced us because you were sneaking around!

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.850
Inconvenienced? What do you mean?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.990
I just got here.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:49.490
Eh?

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:52.430
If Nagisa isn't the thief, then...

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.340
Ahh!

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:56.830
The antique music box that I put here is gone!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.270
Eh!?

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:01.000
I knew it! The thief was someone else!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.670
I'm going outside to find him!

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.260
That's right! Everyone split up and search for him!

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.040
Wait!

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.140
I feel an evil presence.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.910
Yes, it's that shadow.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.260
This is the real burglar.

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.140
He's close, very close.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:21.170
The real burglar is... him!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.730
The burglar's identity was a bunch of stray cats stealing fish?

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:35.340
They really are cat burglars.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.030
Then why is the music box missing?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:42.940
Come on! Who stole it?

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.820
Give back my music box!

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.160
I knew it. It isn't here either.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.580
Kaito...

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:34.830
Lucia.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.160
Why are you here?

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:46.640
Well, I was in the area and I saw the lights were on.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.410
How about you? Why are you here?

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.040
I was just getting some of my fall clothing.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.050
By the way, what are you doing in the middle of the night?

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.670
Ah! I forgot! The thief!

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:03.200
She's weird as usual.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:13.600
Wasn't that Lucia-chan just now? Why did she come to Kaito's home?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:25.880
Could it be that Kaito went home to see Lucia-chan?

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.030
What is this?

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.010
It's scary how the weather changed so suddenly.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.700
Could this be Mikeru's doing?

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:58.380
What a dull feeling... They're evil...

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:01.220
Wait, Mikeru-sama!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:06.470
You shouldn't do this! If you do, you'll just waste your energy!

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:09.150
It'll all end soon...

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:11.100
Mikeru-sama!

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:14.670
I knew it was you! You stubborn chicken!

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:20.350
Mermaid Princess! You're an idiot to face us even now!

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.020
Oh no!

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.360
Lucia!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:33.670
Are you okay?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.220
Hang in there!

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.780
Rina, Hanon... Mikeru is...

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.020
Mikeru?

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.730
What a dull feeling...

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.890
Memories? What are you talking about?

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.240
They're evil.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.160
Huh? What's he saying?

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.650
I don't know. He arrived already like that.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.950
Lucia, Hanon. Let's go.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:58.400
Okay!

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.550
Pink Pearl Voice!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.940
Aqua Pearl Voice!

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.240
Green Pearl Voice!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.450
Pull yourself together, Mikeru-sama!

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.200
That's enough, Mikeru!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:32.680
When you show up, the peace of the seas is disrupted!

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:35.410
We're going to send you packing now!

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.770
Pichi Pichi Voice Live Start!

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.670
Love Shower Pitch!

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:54.590
Where am I?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.970
How about an encore?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:01.170
H-How could this{that} be? That kind of song is supposed to have no effect on Mikeru-sama!

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.950
Why am I here?

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.760
What in the world did I do?

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:09.690
M-Mikeru-sama! Please calm down!

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:12.450
M-Mikeru-sama!

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:20.270
T-This is bad. I'd better use what the Great One gave me.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:29.650
A-Are you okay, Mikeru-sama?

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:32.350
Mikeru.

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:35.210
It's the Mermaid Princesses...

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:39.140
It's not normal for Mikeru to lose himself like that.{It's not normal to lose your sense of self like that.}

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.900
Maybe you should consult us on why that happened.

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:45.560
You saw it all, you eyesores.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:46.800
Begone!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.090
Awww. Told you so.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.870
I'll let you go this time.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.860
That's because I can come take your powers at any time.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:17.750
Plus, I'll tell you now that I will never lose my sense of self like this again.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.940
You can look forward to that, Mermaid Princesses.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:26.910
Mikeru-sama is just beginning to use his true power.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.200
We almost lost our lives there.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.620
But why was Mikeru suffering like that?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.350
Who knows?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.030
The pain of not being able to control yourself...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.010
What in the world is happening to Mikeru?

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:08.860
Father.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.550
I want to forget about you forever.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.670
In the end, we never did find the burglar.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:24.140
And it was right after Rihito-san gave me the music box.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:26.160
Rihito-san.

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:31.330
Rihito-san, what's wrong? Why are you here?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.310
Ahh! The music box!

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:36.420
But why, Rihito-san?

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.360
I'm sorry.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:49.330
This was inside the music box.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:50.950
A letter?

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.320
It's from my father.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:53.270
From your father?

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.970
I want to forget about the past.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:02.620
How could you burn your father's letter?

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:10.330
I would like for Mikaru never to see the contents of the letter he wrote.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:18.150
But it's like you're burning your memories of your father.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:28.090
No matter how beautiful or warm some memories are, there are many others that are best left forgotten.

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:32.030
Many people have suffered because of their memories.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:40.180
By burning those memories to ash, people will be happier.

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:41.580
How could that be?

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:45.120
But, Rihito-san, I...

00:21:55.780 --> 00:22:02.330
I pray that the memories between you and Kaito-kun will never burn to ash and disappear.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:14.030
Kaito, don't go.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:17.950
Stay at my side, Kaito.

00:23:51.150 --> 00:23:55.430
Whenever Kaito and Mikaru are together, they make a good couple.

00:23:55.430 --> 00:23:59.750
Lucia, I've decided to return to my own place.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:02.610
Why are you telling me about this in particular?

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:03.400
I don't know.

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:08.360
But I felt that I needed to tell you about this.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:11.150
Kaito, are you leaving Mikaru's house{home}?

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:14.650
Next time on Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch Pure:

00:24:14.650 --> 00:24:16.360
The Heart Within the Heart.

00:24:16.360 --> 00:24:19.250
Kaito, why are you going back with Mikaru?
